error: invalid function definition parameter list: `b`
 --> sema3-parameter-list.c:1:14
  |
1 | int f(a) int b; { return 0; }
  |              ^ invalid parameter list for a definition
  |
  = note: C99 §6.9.1p5-6: prototype definitions have no declaration list; identifier-list declarations name only listed parameters, with no initializers

error: parameter was not declared, defaults to `int`: `a` [-Wimplicit-int]
 --> sema3-parameter-list.c:1:7
  |
1 | int f(a) int b; { return 0; }
  |       ^ undeclared parameter
  |
  = note: C99 §6.9.1p6: every identifier in the identifier list shall be declared; C89 defaulted to `int`

warning: a function definition without a prototype is deprecated in all versions of C and is not supported in C23 [-Wdeprecated-non-prototype]
 --> sema3-parameter-list.c:1:5
  |
1 | int f(a) int b; { return 0; }
  |     ^ no prototype
  |
  = note: C99 §6.11.6-§6.11.7: empty parentheses in a function declarator and identifier lists in a definition are obsolescent; C23 removes both

2 errors and 1 warning generated.
